-- Clean up the species catalog and add photos.
--
-- 1. Botanical names: genus capitalised, epithet lower case, cultivar in
--    single quotes; misspellings fixed (e.g. "Zamioculcas Zamifolia" ->
--    "Zamioculcas zamiifolia", "Pilea Peperomiodes" -> "Pilea peperomioides").
--    Familiar genus names used in shops are kept (Sansevieria, Calathea,
--    Schefflera) even where botanists now use another genus, so that search
--    finds them.
-- 2. Photos: the free-licence lead image of the matching English Wikipedia
--    article, served from Wikimedia Commons (640 px thumbnail), with author,
--    licence and a link to the file page. 91 of 93 species have a photo.
--    For cultivars and some trade names the photo shows the species or the
--    genus, not the exact cultivar. No photo: Dracaena marginata (Wikipedia
--    redirects to another species) and Sansevieria volkensii (no free image).
--    Four files have no author in their metadata; their attribution says
--    "Unknown author (see source)" and the source link names the author.
--
-- Status: TO VERIFY (names and photo choice). Retrieved 2026-11-18.
-- Never edit this migration after it has been applied; add a new one.

